sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch05-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Network systems whose rewiring rules depend only on whether a node's two connections lead to the same node always grow in an essentially repetitive way, but when rules depend on nodes up to two connections away, even the number of nodes can vary in an apparently random way (in about one in 10,000 rules).";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Network rules depending on distance-two neighborhoods can give random growth";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 5, “Two Dimensions and Beyond”; section “Network Systems” (from p. 193), p. 201. Scope: network systems with local rewiring and node-insertion rules"
}
